===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sarcastic]] [[remark]].
#* Shakespeare
#*: I thank thee for that '''gird''', good Tranio.
# A stroke with a rod or switch.
# A severe spasm; a twinge; a pang.
#* Tillotson
#*: Conscience {{...}} is freed from many fearful '''girds''' and twinges which the atheist feels.

